# ── secrets: never commit secret material ─────────────────────────────────────
# Config references secrets at runtime instead of containing them. One `op inject`
# into a gitignored ~/.secrets at bootstrap, then shells source it.
**/auth.json
**/.secrets
**/secrets.*
*.age
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/.netrc
**/.pgpass

# Token caches. The pattern below is deliberately broad. The previous rule named
# `windows/.config/spotify-tui/client.yml`, but the committed path was
# `windows/.config/archived/spotify-tui/client.yml`. One missing path segment meant
# the rule never applied, and live Spotify credentials were committed and pushed.
# Match on filename, not location.
**/client.yml
**/.spotify_token_cache.json
**/*token_cache*

# ── data that is never config ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~/.local/share/atuin/history.db is ~7 MB of every command ever entered on this
# machine. Shell history is data, and atuin sync is its answer — see
# openspec/backlog/atuin-history-sync.md.
**/.local/share/atuin/
**/history.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/.zsh_history
**/.bash_history
**/.python_history
**/.psql_history
**/.node_repl_history

# ── chezmoi local state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lives outside the repo (~/.config/chezmoi); ignore any stray copy. This section
# goes away entirely at task 8.2.
.chezmoistate*

# ── OS / editor noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Removed 2026-08-27: ~60 entries for the `windows/`, `wsl/`, `ubuntu/`, and
# `ubuntu-and-wsl/` trees. Those directories were deleted by the June 2026 chezmoi
# migration, except `windows/`, which task 3.14 removes. Rules for paths that no
# longer exist hid the fact that `windows/` was still tracked.

# ── installer-owned files: never track these ──────────────────────────────────
# Rescued from home/.chezmoiignore before task 8.1 deleted it. That file's first
# two sections were the per-OS split, now the os/ directories. This third section
# was the only record of WHICH files belong to an installer rather than to us.
#
# herdr and plannotator write these themselves and overwrite them on every update.
# Each carries a "managed by <tool>, updating overwrites this" header. Tracking any
# of them meant drift on every upstream version bump, and a restore offering to put
# the older version back. Recreated on a new machine by `herdr integration install
# <target>` and plannotator's own installer, both of which bin/install-packages runs.
**/.claude/hooks/herdr-agent-state.sh
**/.pi/agent/extensions/herdr-agent-state.ts
**/.omp/agent/extensions/herdr-omp-agent-state.ts
**/.config/opencode/plugins/herdr-agent-state.js
**/.cursor/herdr-agent-state.sh
**/.claude/skills/plannotator-annotate
**/.claude/skills/plannotator-last
**/.claude/skills/plannotator-review

# App-managed STATE, never hand-edited config. The app rewrites these constantly,
# so tracking them is perpetual drift. lazyvim.json holds only news-read hashes and
# install_version — the real config is lua/config/lazy.lua, which IS tracked. Do not
# re-add lazyvim.json.
#
# The rule: a file belongs here only if it holds ZERO config you would want on
# another machine. Anything holding tooling or preferences (like .pi/agent/settings.json,
# which carries provider, model and packages) is source of truth and stays tracked.
**/.config/nvim/lazyvim.json

# Embedded repo internals — never deploy a nested .git. An accidental add of an
# agent's working tree once slurped its whole .git. Keep the agent's files, not its repo.
**/.agents/local/ponytail/.git
**/.agents/local/ponytail/.git/**

# cliamp — Spotify credentials and the client_id that pairs with them. This repo
# is cloned onto a work machine; neither belongs in it.
.config/cliamp/

# Python bytecode next to scripts in os/linux/.local/bin (yt imports itself as a module)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
